From: ZeroCode321 <ZeroCode321@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:20:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(chest): sidebar chest section, '@' source, and .chest
 sharing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The sidebar section is a fold: the header opens the `plugin` and `skill`
groups, and the choice persists in localStorage. A row opens a dialog carrying
every action — install or uninstall, move, export, delete — because a sidebar
column is too narrow to hang five buttons off every line. The plugin inventory
supplies the live module names, which is how a row tells "installed and running"
from "installed, restart to apply".

The '@' source picks differently per kind: a skill lands the `/name` reference
the skill pipeline already understands, and a plugin lands its package
directory, because a plugin is code the agent works on rather than text it acts
out. Copy carries no emoji; every glyph is an icon atom.
